From: Holodor <holodor@bonesaw.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250: add the AOSS cluster sleep state

sm8250.dtsi describes one cluster idle state, cluster-sleep-0 (PSCI
parameter 0x4100c244).  sm8350, sm8450 and sm8550 additionally describe
cluster-sleep-1 with parameter 0x4100c344, the state in which the AOSS is
asked to put the SoC to sleep (CX collapse, DDR self-refresh).  Without a
state that requests it, suspend-to-idle on the Retroid Pocket 5 (SM8250)
never reaches it: /sys/kernel/debug/qcom_stats shows aosd, cxsd and ddr
counts of 0 across a 6.4 h suspend, while the CPUs power-collapse and the
cluster domain enters cluster-sleep-0 once per suspend; the device drains
~2.5 %/h asleep (measured 2026-10-16).  Add the deeper state as the last
entry of the cluster domain so s2idle picks it.

Latencies are copied from cluster-sleep-0 pending measurement.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
@@ -368,6 +368,14 @@
 				exit-latency-us = <6562>;
 				min-residency-us = <9987>;
 			};
+
+			cluster_sleep_1: cluster-sleep-1 {
+				compatible = "domain-idle-state";
+				arm,psci-suspend-param = <0x4100c344>;
+				entry-latency-us = <3264>;
+				exit-latency-us = <6562>;
+				min-residency-us = <9987>;
+			};
 		};
 	};
 
@@ -745,7 +753,7 @@
 
 		cluster_pd: power-domain-cpu-cluster0 {
 			#power-domain-cells = <0>;
-			domain-idle-states = <&cluster_sleep_0>;
+			domain-idle-states = <&cluster_sleep_0>, <&cluster_sleep_1>;
 		};
 	};
 
